What is Passenger Car Air Suspension?
Passenger Car Air Suspension is an advanced type of vehicle suspension system powered by an electric air compressor. This compressor pumps air into flexible bellows, typically made from textile-reinforced rubber, which inflate to raise the chassis from the axle, providing superior ride quality and customizable comfort settings. These systems offer significant advantages over traditional steel spring suspensions, including improved vibration damping, dynamic ride height adjustment, and enhanced stability control.
Unlike conventional suspension systems that rely on metal springs, air suspension delivers exceptional ride smoothing capabilities and adaptabilty to varying load conditions.
